-- title:
--   The integral Hecke algebra preserves the integral lattice
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, let $k$ be an integer with $1 \le k$, and let $S$ be a set of natural numbers. Let $t$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphism of the space $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ of cusp forms of weight $k$ for `CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N`, and suppose $t$ lies in [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N k S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), that is, in the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the set [`CuspForm.heckeGenerators N k S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L14), which consists of the operators `heckeTLin k hℓ hℓN` for primes $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, together with the operators `heckeULin k hqN` for primes $q$ with $q \mid N$ and $q \notin S$. Let $f$ be a cusp form lying in [`CuspForm.intLattice N k`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3), the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ spanned by those cusp forms $g$ for which every coefficient $\mathrm{qCoeff}\, g\, n$, the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $g$ with respect to width $1$, is the image of an integer in $\mathbb{C}$. Then $t f$ again lies in [`CuspForm.intLattice N k`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3).
--
--   This is the integrality statement that the anemic Hecke algebra over $\mathbb{Z}$ acts on the lattice of cusp forms with integral $q$-expansion. It underlies the finiteness of the Hecke algebra as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module and the construction of eigenvectors for characters of the Hecke algebra, through [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure.moduleFinite_heckeAlgebra`](thm.html#CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure.moduleFinite_heckeAlgebra) and [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure.exists_ne_zero_forall_apply_eq_smul`](thm.html#CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure.exists_ne_zero_forall_apply_eq_smul).
